        <body>
            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0601" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg539"/>

                <head>No. 337.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 10, 1878</date>.
                        (Received February 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 660.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your dispatch No. 432, of the
                    7th ultimo, making inquiry whether any of the assailants of the Rio Grande City
                    jail had been arrested, tried, or punished in Mexico in accordance with the
                    penal code, I have to report that, in a call which I made at the foreign office
                    on the 26th ultimo, I directed Mr. Vallarta’s attention to the inquiry, and left
                    with him a copy of your dispatch.</p>
                <p>Under date of the 7th instant I received from Mr. Vallarta to-day a “verbal
                    note,” of which I inclose a translation, in reply. The greater portion of the
                    note is occupied with the demand made by Governor Hubbard, of Texas, for the
                    extradition of the parties referred to; but in its conclusion Mr. Vallarta
                    states that he has no information of the arrest, trial, or conviction of the
                    criminals under the penal code, but that he has asked for reports from the
                    authorities of Tamaulipas on the subject.</p>
                <p>I also inclose a copy of my note acknowledging the receipt of Mr. Vallarta’s of
                    the 7th instant.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d342-a1.xml" xpointer="d342-a1"/>
